{
  "$comment": [
    "The repository entries of a team's capture policy: how the account service stores each one and how terma-cli reads it.",
    "Byte-identical copies: terma-cli internal/routing/testdata/entry_grammar.json is the source; mirador-platform",
    "account/api/internal/policy/testdata/entry_grammar.json is the copy, which the platform's entry-grammar CI job compares",
    "with terma-cli's main. A change lands here first.",
    "The server stores nothing a released CLI would refuse or read differently, except under a new policy major (as 2.0",
    "did for wildcards): reviewers hold that line, since the job compares with main, not with a release.",
    "server: how the account service stores the entry (validatePolicyRepository, after trimming): exact, wildcard or refused.",
    "cli: how terma-cli's routing.ParseEntry reads it with wildcards on: exact, wildcard or refused. The CLI is the more",
    "lenient reader: it also takes clone URLs, which the server refuses.",
    "Contract, checked on both sides from these two columns: an entry the server stores is never refused by the CLI, and",
    "is a wildcard to both or to neither."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {"entry": "github.com/acme/api", "server": "exact", "cli": "exact"},
    {"entry": "GitHub.com/Owner/Repo.js", "server": "exact", "cli": "exact"},
    {"entry": "gitlab.com/group/sub/app", "server": "exact", "cli": "exact"},
